## Secure defaults

New projects use `func.AuthLevel.FUNCTION` for graph execution routes. In Azure,
send a function key using `x-functions-key`; never put keys in URLs or logs.
Local `func start` does not enforce function keys, so local development is unchanged.

Only for an intentionally public demo, set the generated project's app setting
`LANGGRAPH_PUBLIC_DEMO=true` before startup. This switches graph routes to
`ANONYMOUS` and emits a template-owned Python `UserWarning` during indexing,
visible in local Core Tools host output. Only the exact lowercase string `true`
opts in: `True`, `TRUE`, `1`, `yes`, empty, whitespace and newline variants keep FUNCTION.
Do not enable this setting in production. Existing generated projects are not modified.

A function key is application-level access control, not user identity or per-user
authorization. Configure identity separately and consult the
[LangGraph library documentation](https://github.com/yeongseon/azure-functions-langgraph-python)
for `ThreadAuthorizer` guidance before exposing thread data. Apply request quotas,
model token limits, rate limits and cost alerts at your API gateway/provider.

